{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122190","id":4229998721,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc78IKiB","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122190","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122190.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122190.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122190","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122190/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122190/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122190/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/4b4c5c0fc7b22289849bc433c8b8c123f55b52e7","number":122190,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use sky material for sky radiance instead of fog material","user":{"login":"diomonogatari","id":17832206,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODMyMjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17832206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari","html_url":"https://github.com/diomonogatari","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/diomonogatari/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #122047 \r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe bug happened because the `_get_sky_material_data()` function is trying to do two different jobs at the same time.\r\n\r\nAfter PR #110956, ENV_BG_COLOR/ENV_BG_CLEAR_COLOR selected `fog_material`, which is correct for drawing the background with `_draw_sky` but for radiance updates in `_update_sky_radiance` it caused problems.\r\n\r\nBoth paths were sharing `_get_sky_material_data()`, so radiance accidentally used `fog_material` in `BG_COLOR`. That made sky radiance black/incorrect, which made ambient/reflections look unlit.\r\n\r\nThis fix separates those responsibilities (`BACKGROUND` vs `RADIANCE`) so each path gets the correct material.\r\n\r\nI've used the mrp attached to this issue to test the changes\r\n[Screencast_20260807_171610.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b892b2eb-b8c5-4d99-821d-6e1d854cbd25)\r\n\r\n\r\n## AI Disclosure\r\nI've used ChatGPT free to navigate through the problem regarding computer graphics / game engines problem space as this is new to me and I come from a backend world.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","col